ng the mathematician's method of analyzing life and exposing the hard-won insights of the academic community to the layman--minus the jargon. Ellenberg pulls from history as well as from the latest theoretical developments to provide those not trained in math with the knowledge they need.\"--\n# How not to be wrong :\n\n## APA\n\nEllenberg J., . (2014). How not to be wrong. New York: The Penguin Press.\n\n## Chicago\n\nEllenberg Jordan, . 2014. How not to be wrong. New York: The Penguin Press.\n\n## Harvard\n\nEllenberg J., . (2014). How not to be wrong. New York: The Penguin Press.\n\n## MLA\n\nEllenberg Jordan, . How not to be wrong. New York: The Penguin Press. 2014.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow not to be wrong : the power of mathematical thinking | Tritonia - Tria | Finna.fi (https://www.finna.fi/Record/tria.316341)\nciteturn36search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; \n\n# How not to be wrong : the power of mathematical thinking\n\nImage\n\nImage: QR Code\n\nFinna rating\n\n[Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\n\nBe the first to leave a review. All reviews are public.\n\nBook , bound\n\nEllenberg, Jordan , kirjoittaja\n\n## Ellenberg, Jordan\n\nSearch as author Search as topic\n\nClose\n\nPenguin Press 2014.\n\nSaved in:\n\nOther Titles  | Power of mathematical thinking\nPhysical Description  | 468 pages : illustrations ; 25 cm\nLanguage  | English\nPublisher  | New York (N.Y.) : Penguin Press, 2014.\nClassification  | udkx 51\nSubjects  | Mathematics.\nAdditional Information  | Jordan Ellenberg\nBibliography  | Includes bibliographical references and index.\nISBN  | 1-59420-522-1 sidottu\n978-1-59420-522-4 sidottu\n\n## Material provided by 5 libraries\n\n  * Tritonia - Tria\n    *     * Any questions or feedback related to the material?\n    * Contact us\n\n  * HAMK University of Applied Sciences Library of Parliament University of Eastern Finla