he the Soviets (with fake instrument panel photos, faked speed, altitude and so on values), to a project code-named Suntan, — a hydrogen-powered replacement for the U-2 in 1957 that was classified above top secret (but never went to completion — just so you know there are classifications above “Top” secret) to a 1959 incident in which a Taiwanese pilot, being trained by the CIA, ‘flamed out’ while on a flight, and made an emergency landing at a small county airport at dusk — imagine being the airport’s manager, seeing a weird-looking craft land, after which an almond-eyed, space-suited being jumped out, ran over to you shouting in barely passable English, “Quick! --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBibliographies: 'Lockheed' – Grafiati (https://www.grafiati.com/en/literature-selections/lockheed/)\nciteturn36search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; \n\n7\n\nM, Bowers Peter, ed. Lockheed Constellation. Motorbooks International, 1992.\n\nFind full text\n\nAdd to bibliography\n\nAPA, Harvard, Vancouver, ISO, and other styles\n\n8\n\nBirtles, Philip. Lockheed L1011 tristar. MBI Pub. Co., 1998.\n\nFind full text\n\nAdd to bibliography\n\nAPA, Harvard, Vancouver, ISO, and other styles\n\n9\n\nWixey, Kenneth E. The Lockheed Constellation. Tempus, 2001.\n\nFind full text\n\nAdd to bibliography\n\nAPA, Harvard, Vancouver, ISO, and other styles\n\n10\n\nPace, Steve. Lockheed Skunk Works. Motorbooks International, 1992.\n\nFind full text\n\nAdd to bibliography\n\nAPA, Harvard, Vancouver, ISO, and other styles\n\nMore sources\n\n## Book chapters on the topic \"Lockheed\"\n\n1\n\nCiceker, Mesut. \"A Contribution from Lockheed Martin.\" In Aerospace Technologies and Applications for Dual Use. River Publishers, 2022. http://dx.doi.org/10.1201/9781003337133-36.\n\nFull text\n\nAdd to bibliography\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n.250. |a2nd ed., Random tr